" vim: filetype=vim
" https://github.com/tridactyl/tridactyl/wiki/Exemplar-.tridactylrc-files

" This wipes all existing settings. This means that if a setting in this file
" is removed, then it will return to default. In other words, this file serves
" as an enforced single point of truth for Tridactyl's configuration.
sanitize tridactyllocal tridactylsync

" Set the theme
colourscheme --url https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devnullvoid/tridactyl/main/themes/catppuccin-machiatto.css catppuccin-mocha

" Just use a blank page for new tab. It would be nicer to use the standard
" Firefox homepage, but Tridactyl doesn't support this yet.
set newtab about:blank

" Use vim in tmux for editor.
" set editorcmd terminal -e tmux -u new vim -S /home/andrew/.vim/tridactyl.vim
set editorcmd xdg-terminal-exec --app-id=term-tridactyl -e nvim

" Ctrl-F should use the browser's native 'find' functionality.
unbind <C-f>

" Ctrl-I is for page settings!
unbind <C-i>
unbind <C-I>

" But also support Tridactyl search too.
bind / fillcmdline find
bind ? fillcmdline find -?
bind n findnext 1
bind N findnext -1
" Remove search highlighting.
bind ,<Space> nohlsearch

" Use sensitive case. Smart case would be nice here, but it doesn't work.
" set findcase sensitive
" Smooth scrolling, yes please. This is still a bit janky in Tridactyl.
set smoothscroll true

" The default jump of 10 is a bit much.
bind j scrollline 5
bind k scrollline -5

" K and J should move between tabs. x should close them.
bind J tabnext
bind K tabprev
bind x tabclose

" Don't run Tridactyl on some web sites because it doesn't work well, or
" because the web site has its own keybindings.
autocmd DocStart mail.google.com mode ignore
autocmd DocStart localhost mode ignore

" Sometimes the status bar in the bottom left corner overlaps the Tridactyl
" command line, so set an option to move the status bar to the right.
guiset_quiet hoverlink right

" Notion links clicked inside the browser go to the Notion app (url-open owns the
" predicate; the hook only asks). DocStart, not BeforeRequest: webRequest URLs are
" stripped of the #block fragment, tri.contentLocation.href keeps it, so the app
" opens the block that was clicked. Cost: the page starts loading before we decide.
" We never close the browser tab: the app opens alongside it, on purpose, so a tab
" reached by clicking through (not opened fresh) keeps its history and can still
" be navigated back. Fails open — not-ours (exit 3) or a dead native messenger
" leaves the tab loading exactly as it would without this hook.
autocmd DocStart ^https://((www\.)?notion\.so|app\.notion\.com)/ js tri.native.run("\"$HOME/.local/bin/url-open\" --route-stdin", tri.contentLocation.href).catch(() => 0)

" Linear workspace links use the router's path allowlist; preserve the browser tab.
autocmd DocStart ^https://linear\.app/ js tri.native.run("\"$HOME/.local/bin/url-open\" --route-stdin", tri.contentLocation.href).catch(() => 0)

" Meet uses PWAsForFirefox's native auto-launch instead: enabled URL handler
" https://meet.google.com/ on the Meet site, plus the extension's auto-launch switch.
" It intercepts before page load and closes only newly created navigation tabs.
" Do not add a Meet DocStart hook here: it would duplicate the native handoff.

